A||N||16||Soelas||Jumping a Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||Soelas||07-14-2001||02:26 PM||||Several months ago I was in a rush to get my GF to work. In my attempts to save time during rush hour traffic, I sped down a (well known to me) side street behind some industrial buildings. near the end of this side street I had forgotten that there was several sets of railroad tracks which were somewhat (use your imagination) raised. About  100 feet before the tracks I had checked my speed. I was doing 90kph (approx 55mph). I looked over and saw the railways crossing signs and gasped as I launched.<P>In all approximations, I probably got about a foot to a foot and a half of air. and Just about cleared the tracks (15 to 20 feet).....(If I was going faster I probably would've cleared them and had a softer landing). I landed hard, (skid marks on the engine cradle, oil pan, tranny and underbody) and shortly thereafter noticed a really bad vibration sound when my drive train wasn't under load.<P>After some diagnosing.... it seemed to be a slipped main bearing <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">. So now, I'm on my way to putting in a v8 using one of Archie's kits.<P>I just wanted you all to know that my '84 2m4 did NOT stand up too well to that sort of abuse......but I may take the jump again when I can afford to trash another car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Soelas<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||07-14-2001||02:35 PM||||Ouch-O. Fiero's can swim, but they can't fly. That really sucks. The only car I suggest for jumping is a Chevette. Just leave the pile of twisted metal where it skidded to a halt and buy a new one.||||reg||9
Z||000002||grinthock||07-14-2001||02:51 PM||||When I first turned 16 I jumped my parents SUV at LEAST 3 feet in the air, scared the SH1T out of me!!!!!  Landed heavy, bounced and I almost lost control.....<P>Bottom line?  <P><BR>I would NEVER EVER EVER EVER consider jumping ANY vehicle again.<P>Learn from this --- DONT do it... Consider that if you even have the steering wheel a HAIR too far left/right you could have rolled.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||07-14-2001||07:02 PM||||I would not say jumped, but I did catch major air in a 79 Olds Regency 98 when I drove off the top of a cloverleaf. I was driving in the rain on bad tires when I tried to make the onramp from the overpass. I launched the car off the top of the ramp, punching a hole the size of the front of the cat through the 4x6 signpost that was holding up the warning sign. The guy behind me who stopped to help said my car had at least six feet of daylight under it. I landed safely, not even denting that Detroit tank. Of ourse, I did have a pretty nasty front end problem after that.  But if I were to go dredevil, one of them body on frame fullsize GM's would definately be my pick...||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroHeather||07-14-2001||07:21 PM||||Grinthock used to take me down this one road where the right hand side of the railway tracks had this wicked slope.  In the old clunker of an SUV, he'd be going like 90mph over the tracks sending me airborne in the passenger side!  I hit my head every time (he thought that was funny!).  From now on, even in my parents mini-van, I hold on to the handle on the roof, or the roof itself to brace myself for the bump, even though the township has pretty much fixed it.  It was pretty cool though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||2
Z||000005||Soelas||07-14-2001||08:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>Ouch-O. Fiero's can swim, but they can't fly. That really sucks. The only car I suggest for jumping is a Chevette. Just leave the pile of twisted metal where it skidded to a halt and buy a new one.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Fiero's can swim?? hmmmm...I wonder if there's an outboard motor attachment for Fiero that I can buy......  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>btw..Fiero's CAN fly....they just aren't so good at the landing part. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I FULLY believe if I was going faster I would've cleared the tracks entirely and landed MUCH smoother than landing right SMACK on top of the high spot on the second set of tracks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.||||reg||1
Z||000006||8Ball||07-14-2001||08:52 PM||||Ahh the Joy of railroad tracks.<P>I Was out in a Celebrity (of all things) I owned one day with 3 friends. We were going swimming at our favorite Quarry. Well the little road leading to it is very windy and has some railroad track in the middle of a curve. I was doing prolly about 60 going down this road. We loved to get the car sideways and had been doing so for years. (Dangerous I know but have never had a single wreck)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">But this time I did not slow for the tracks and when we hit them in the middle of the slide the car went up on 2 wheels!!! WAY UP!! My then g/f looked out the side window almost straight out and saw the pavement. But Sean and I were haveing a blast!!! well I managed to drive the car around the next to back to back 25 degree turns and in the straight away and landed it back when I lost speed.<P>I know it sounds unbelieveable and I wouldn't believe me but I have 3 witness'  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sorry so long but just wanted to share<P>8Ball||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroBUZZ||07-14-2001||10:43 PM||||Way back when I was young, I had the only Fiat 124 Spider in Cape Breton, NS.  I babied that thing until I took it to Halifax for a service.  Two young Italian guys had a shop and I went out for a ride with one of them.  He jumped a RR crossing at speed, all the while saying 'is a bootifull engeen' Scared the crap out of me.<P>I put 75,000 miles on it in a year and a half and I think I hit the 6500 RPM redline just about every shift after that ride.<P>Gary||||reg||6
Z||000008||The Fieromaster||07-14-2001||11:46 PM||||Actually... you know what flys well?  A 84 Honda Civic!  My winter beater was a 84 Civic and I used to launch a local set of tracks that are HELLA steep!  The wild part... I did it at 80 mph!  Talk about air... I could get about 5' vertical and 15 or so feet in length!  I will get pics of the tracks sometime and all the chuncks of street missing from the landings... I jumped one time and a person was in the other lane... I thought her jaw was gonna fall off!  OOOPSIE!  Oh well thats what happens when you pay 100$ for a beater!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That, Wrecked Better"<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">      <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||07-15-2001||02:50 AM||||All this time looking at the topic I thought you were talking about how to jump-start a Fiero... hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000010||Galen||07-15-2001||02:57 AM||||hehe.. you would standard  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"It may be the opinion of the court, but its still wrong"</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><A HREF="http://www.ezRpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>ezRpg Networks</A></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fierokid87||07-15-2001||03:41 AM||||Yeah I remember my budy and I were in a rush and we flew past our destination.  so we turned arouns in a parking lot that had a nice dip in it.  And we jumped it.  This was in my old Chevy Citation I drove in High School.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||KRMFiero||07-15-2001||10:03 AM||||I take mine up to about 65mph on this road (Dougles Hook, In Chapachet RI) and there is a huge hill and at the end you can get air with any car/truck.... I dont know how far i go but i ca hear the tires sqeel when i land, I have got air in my friends jeep, moms van, S-10, Honda Accord.... road is fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||jake1852||07-15-2001||10:14 AM||||I jump all my cars. (unless they are in need of shocks!) there is a huge bump down the road with a straight away before it, and the way it it set up, it is smooth as hell. only problem is that you cant see whats coming from the other side. i have yet to have a mid-air collision with someont though!<P>------------------<BR>- Unfinished ferrari kit, custom made myself<BR>-87 duke (just got it, its fast, and i dont know why yet!)<BR>- 87 GT<BR>- Tc Maserati (daily drive)||||reg||1
Z||000014||Seanh||07-15-2001||01:41 PM||||Just recently I found a really nice jump spot before RR tracks that I'm going to try  it with the Fiero once its all complete and broken in. I took it over it a few times before my red-headed step child wrecked it, but I always hit it from the other direction, so actually the ground falls out from under the car. One time I had my sunroof out and at one time my chin was above the roof line it fell so quickly. <P>Theres a really big dip on a steet near our school. When I rebuilt the Fiero, I was driving the Bronco for a few months. I loved hitting that dip with the truck. It was rather painful landing. And there was one kid in the truck that was at the time in the backseat, he stuck his head up front when I said were going to hit it, and just stayed there yelling "Oh **** " over and over again until we were on the ground once again. I also had the truck full of crap like chains and tools, oil, all things you could possibly need, its kinda cool when you just see everything floating in mid air, then you hit the ground and it all falls and scares the ****  outta ya.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 4spd Auto (Currently in repair, wrecked by "Red-Headed Step Child")<BR><I>I live my life a 1/4 mile at a time. Nothing else matters</I>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Huck||07-18-2001||06:46 PM||||I take pride in being able to say I have caught air in:<P>1.  86 Chev 4x4<BR>2.  89 Buick Park Ave.<BR>3.  89 Chev 4x4<BR>4.  89 Jeep Cherokee (doesnt fly well)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>5.  95 Chev 1/2 ton<BR>6.  89 Chev Safari (again, doesnt fly well)<BR>7.  86 Fiero 2m4<BR>8.  87 Fiero GT<P>All flew on a local road called rollercoaster road... 1.5 lane gravel no winter maintenance road.... gotta go about 120 - 140km/h depending what your driving...  and oh yeah, ALWAYS get a friend to sit at the end of the road and block oncoming traffic!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Huck||||reg||1
Z||000016||Cheever2||07-18-2001||06:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Soelas:<BR>Fiero's can swim??<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I was able to drive my GT thru water over the hood and touching the bottom of the windshield, in the Allison flood here.  I don't know how the engine was able to breath through the stock intake.<P>I used to frequently get my Scout SSII over 6 feet into the air at the Arkansas riverbed in Tulsa.  Landed on soft sand.  The suspension was beefed: I had a leaf added and had them re-arched for a little lift, with KYB gas-adjust shocks.  A guy who took pictures of it in the air lost the photos.<P>||||reg||1
